Recursion is when a function calls itself to solve a smaller version of the same problem. The classic example is factorial:
```python
def fact(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return n * fact(n - 1)
```
Every recursion needs a base case so it eventually stops.

```javascript
function greet(name) {
  return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
console.log(greet("world"));
```
You can also write it as an arrow function: `const greet = (name) => `Hello, ${name}!`;`.
